# AlloyGraph configuration.
#
# Copy to .env IN THE REPOSITORY ROOT -- that is the only location the
# application reads. Both the backend (backend/alloy_crew/agents.py) and the
# evaluation harness resolve this path from their own file location, so it does
# not matter which directory you launch from.
#
# .env is gitignored and must never be committed.

# --- LLM provider (at least one required) -------------------------------------
# The agents resolve providers in this order and use the first with a usable
# key: DeepInfra, Together AI, Groq, OpenAI. With none set they fall back to a
# local Ollama model, which is only useful if you have actually installed one.
#
# Research Chat resolves the SAME order via an OpenAI-compatible client
# (backend/services/config.py -> alloy_crew.agents.resolve_chat_endpoint), so
# one key configures all three modes.
DEEPINFRA_API_KEY=
# TOGETHER_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=          # Groq withdrew llama-3.3-70b-versatile on 2026-08-16

# Only consulted when no key above is usable. Unset means chat reports that no
# provider is configured rather than silently answering from an 8B local model.
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434

# Optional overrides, mainly for reproducing evaluation runs.
# ALLOYGRAPH_LLM_MODEL=
# ALLOYGRAPH_LLM_TEMPERATURE=

# --- Services -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Defaults match docker-compose; set these only if you run them elsewhere.
# WEAVIATE_URL=http://localhost:8081
# GRAPHDB_URL=http://localhost:7200
